research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-122-### 2. `cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero` — class (a)
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-123-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-124-The first Remark currently says that in the explicit rational cover “every one of those intervals meets every other.” The intervals are centred at an arbitrary enumeration of the rationals with rapidly decreasing radii; two sufficiently separated intervals need not intersect. Density of their union follows because the union contains every rational and is independent of pairwise intersection.
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-125-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-126-Proposed replacement:
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-127-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-128-> `For every ε > 0 the rationals are covered by open intervals of total length exactly ε ([[ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length]]), although their union is dense.`
