research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-395-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-396-**Given:** The set $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ of rationals inside $\mathbb{R}$ and its complement $X = \mathbb{R} \setminus \mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-397-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-398-[A1] The refuted claim: $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is $G_\delta$, equivalently $X$ is $F_\sigma$.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-399-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md:400:[L1] $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is $F_\sigma$ and meager, $X$ is $G_\delta$ and residual, and $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is not $G_\delta$ ([[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]], claims 1, 2, 3).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-401-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-q-is-g-delta.md-402-[L2] $A$ is $F_\sigma$ if and only if $\mathbb{R} \setminus A$ is $G_\delta$ ([[def-f-sigma-g-delta]], [[def-open-and-closed-in-r]]).
