research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-1399-  many singletons, each of which *is* nowhere dense
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md:1400:  ([[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]]). So the failure above is not a failure of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-1401-  topological smallness in every sense: it is exactly the failure of the
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-1402-  one-step condition. Meagreness is the countable-union closure of nowhere
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-1403-  density, and it is the notion under which $\mathbb{Q}$ is small.
