research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2602-  selections are two instantiations. Nothing on this page uses the countably
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2603-  infinite version, and every meager set met below is presented together with an
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2604-  explicit witnessing sequence.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2605-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2606-- **Nowhere dense is strictly stronger than having empty interior.**
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2607-  $\mathbb{Q}$ has empty interior, since no neighbourhood consists of rationals
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2608-  alone, yet $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{R}$ has interior $\mathbb{R}$, so
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2609-  $\mathbb{Q}$ is not nowhere dense. It is nevertheless meager, being a union of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md:2610:  singletons; that computation is [[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]].
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2611-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2612-- **First category, second category and residual are not a trichotomy.** A set
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2613-  is meager or of the second category, and those two are exhaustive and
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2614-  exclusive by definition. Residual is a separate condition on the complement: a
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2615-  residual set is of the second category once $\mathbb{R}$ is known not to be
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2616-  meager in itself ([[thm-baire-category-r]]), but before that theorem nothing
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2617-  rules out a set that is both meager and residual.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-2618-
