research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-670-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-671-- **The classes are genuinely larger than the closed and the open sets.**
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-672-  $\mathbb{Q}$ is $F_\sigma$ and is neither open nor closed, and the irrationals
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-673-  are $G_\delta$ and neither open nor closed; both computations are in
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md:674:  [[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]]. That $\mathbb{Q}$ is not also $G_\delta$
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-675-  is the first genuinely hard fact about these classes and needs the Baire
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-676-  category theorem ([[thm-baire-category-r]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-677-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-q-is-g-delta.prompt.md-678-- **Why the algebra of open sets is not enough.** [[thm-open-set-algebra-r]]
