research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1449-  selections are two instantiations. Nothing on this page uses the countably
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1450-  infinite version, and every meager set met below is presented together with an
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1451-  explicit witnessing sequence.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1452-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1453-- **Nowhere dense is strictly stronger than having empty interior.**
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1454-  $\mathbb{Q}$ has empty interior, since no neighbourhood consists of rationals
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1455-  alone, yet $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{R}$ has interior $\mathbb{R}$, so
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1456-  $\mathbb{Q}$ is not nowhere dense. It is nevertheless meager, being a union of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md:1457:  singletons; that computation is [[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]].
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1458-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1459-- **First category, second category and residual are not a trichotomy.** A set
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1460-  is meager or of the second category, and those two are exhaustive and
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1461-  exclusive by definition. Residual is a separate condition on the complement: a
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1462-  residual set is of the second category once $\mathbb{R}$ is known not to be
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1463-  meager in itself ([[thm-baire-category-r]]), but before that theorem nothing
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1464-  rules out a set that is both meager and residual.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-baire-reproves-r-uncountable.prompt.md-1465-
