research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1142-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1143-- **Nowhere dense is strictly stronger than having empty interior.**
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1144-  $\mathbb{Q}$ has empty interior, since no neighbourhood consists of rationals
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1145-  alone, yet $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{R}$ has interior $\mathbb{R}$, so
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1146-  $\mathbb{Q}$ is not nowhere dense. It is nevertheless meager, being a union of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md:1147:  singletons; that computation is [[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]].
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1148-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1149-- **First category, second category and residual are not a trichotomy.** A set
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1150-  is meager or of the second category, and those two are exhaustive and
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1151-  exclusive by definition. Residual is a separate condition on the complement: a
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1152-  residual set is of the second category once $\mathbb{R}$ is known not to be
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1153-  meager in itself ([[thm-baire-category-r]]), but before that theorem nothing
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.prompt.md-1154-  rules out a set that is both meager and residual.
