research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.prompt.md-185-- **Meagre and measure zero are not the same smallness.** $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is both, but the two notions diverge as soon as one leaves the countable case: [[cex-meager-set-of-full-measure]] writes $\mathbb{R}$ as a meager set together with a set of measure zero, and the set of measure zero there is residual. So being residual, which is what claim 2 gives for $X$, carries no information at all about size in measure.
