research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-155-1.2 $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is not nowhere dense: its closure is $\mathbb{R}$ by [L3], and the interior of $\mathbb{R}$ is $\mathbb{R}$ itself by [L4], since $\mathbb{R}$ is an open subset of $\mathbb{R}$; so the interior of the closure is $\mathbb{R} \ne \varnothing$. [L3, L4]
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-156-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-157-2.1 So $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is a subset of $\mathbb{R}$ of measure zero that is not nowhere dense, and the claim [A1] fails at it; the claim is therefore false. [step 1.1, step 1.2, A1] ∎
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-158-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-159-## Remarks
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-160-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-161-- **$\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is nonetheless meager**, being a union of countably
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-162-  many singletons, each of which *is* nowhere dense
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md:163:  ([[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]]). So the failure above is not a failure of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-164-  topological smallness in every sense: it is exactly the failure of the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-165-  one-step condition. Meagreness is the countable-union closure of nowhere
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-166-  density, and it is the notion under which $\mathbb{Q}$ is small.
