research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1253-is extended by $F_n := F_m$ for $n > m$, and a finite list of open sets likewise,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1254-so nothing is lost by indexing over $\mathbb{N}$.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1255-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1256-## Remarks
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1257-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1258-- **The classes are genuinely larger than the closed and the open sets.**
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1259-  $\mathbb{Q}$ is $F_\sigma$ and is neither open nor closed, and the irrationals
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1260-  are $G_\delta$ and neither open nor closed; both computations are in
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md:1261:  [[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]]. That $\mathbb{Q}$ is not also $G_\delta$
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1262-  is the first genuinely hard fact about these classes and needs the Baire
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1263-  category theorem ([[thm-baire-category-r]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1264-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1265-- **Why the algebra of open sets is not enough.** [[thm-open-set-algebra-r]]
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1266-  gives that a *finite* intersection of open sets is open and a *finite* union of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1267-  closed sets is closed. The definitions above are exactly what one gets by
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1268-  relaxing "finite" to "countable" once, and the point of the whole notion is
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1269-  that the relaxation is proper: a countable intersection of open sets need not
--
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1808-  selections are two instantiations. Nothing on this page uses the countably
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1809-  infinite version, and every meager set met below is presented together with an
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1810-  explicit witnessing sequence.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1811-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1812-- **Nowhere dense is strictly stronger than having empty interior.**
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1813-  $\mathbb{Q}$ has empty interior, since no neighbourhood consists of rationals
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1814-  alone, yet $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathbb{R}$ has interior $\mathbb{R}$, so
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1815-  $\mathbb{Q}$ is not nowhere dense. It is nevertheless meager, being a union of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md:1816:  singletons; that computation is [[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]].
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1817-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1818-- **First category, second category and residual are not a trichotomy.** A set
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1819-  is meager or of the second category, and those two are exhaustive and
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1820-  exclusive by definition. Residual is a separate condition on the complement: a
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1821-  residual set is of the second category once $\mathbb{R}$ is known not to be
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1822-  meager in itself ([[thm-baire-category-r]]), but before that theorem nothing
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1823-  rules out a set that is both meager and residual.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta.md-1824-
