research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log:273679:-{"id":"cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Book%3A_Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps/6.8.E%3A_Problems_on_Baire_Categories_and_Linear_Maps","https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps"],"rationale":"Zakon records that the rationals are meager and not G-delta and that a dense G-delta in a complete metric space is residual. The local item packages the complementary F-sigma/G-delta conclusions and supplies its own dependency-local proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-273680--{"id":"def-measure-zero-and-content-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf","https://math.mit.edu/~brubaker/103PSet1Sol.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT materials use the same epsilon-small countable interval-cover definition of nullity and contrast finite covers for compact null sets. The local term content zero is a deliberately elementary finite-cover convention, so the package is a semantic restatement rather than an exact quotation of Jordan measure.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-273681--{"id":"lem-finite-interval-cover-total-length","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/~brubaker/103PSet1Sol.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT solution states and proves that a finite interval cover of a nondegenerate closed interval has total length at least the interval length. The local proof changes the finite-overlap organization but follows the same covering estimate.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-273682--{"id":"lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/~brubaker/103PSet1Sol.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT solution gives exactly that a closed interval of positive length is not a measure-zero set and derives it from compactness and the finite-cover length bound. The local proof follows that argument with this library’s series indexing.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
