research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-297635--{"id":"lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/~brubaker/103PSet1Sol.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT solution gives exactly that a closed interval of positive length is not a measure-zero set and derives it from compactness and the finite-cover length bound. The local proof follows that argument with this library’s series indexing.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
